(Bug #98: `#x` is the obvious typo for hexadecimal - the `#` does not
 belong in Vox's table (the correct form is bare `x`) - and used to
 silently print decimal, which is exactly the "wrong answer" the manual's
 own principle for specifiers forbids (LANGUAGE.md:3293-3295).)

a number called n is 255.
Print "{n:#x}".
